Package: aRchtest
Title: Declare and Enforce Architectural Rules in 'testthat'
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R:
    person("Fabian", "Distler", , "fdistlermpi@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Declare architectural boundaries between the modules of an R
    project as data and enforce them as ordinary 'testthat' tests. Rules are
    built with a small pipe-friendly grammar, checked by static analysis of
    the project's parse data, and reported as located findings naming the
    file, line, enclosing function and offending call. The code under
    analysis is never sourced, loaded or evaluated, so checks are
    deterministic, safe in continuous integration, and work on a project
    that does not currently run.
